{"content_hash": "24f8f6a757b66e02", "version_id": 744, "article_id": 75, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Crowd of 50 beats foreigner to death in Durban", "title_zh": "德班约50人围殴一名外国人致死", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck5yn9z3vnego?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1623438744990-f47414813a29?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Nnx8Y3Jvd2QlMjBiZWF0cyUyMGZvcmVpZ25lcnxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkyNzEzOTg0fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Amir Arabshahi on Unsplash", "author": "Amir Arabshahi", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@amir_arabshahi?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-crowd-of-people-with-their-hands-in-the-air-ERSKz8OrZIQ?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(69, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(107, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "d8d50814b11f"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-23", "word_count": 212, "reading_minutes": 1.1, "lead": "Police in South Africa say a crowd of about 50 people has beaten a foreign national to death in Durban. The killing comes after months of anti-migrant protests, some of which turned violent.", "lead_zh": "南非警方称，德班约50人围殴一名外籍人士致死。这起事件发生在持续数月的反移民抗议之后，部分抗议曾演变为暴力。", "preview": "According to police, the man, who has not been identified, was believed to be in his late 30s or early 40s. Two men first approached him by ", "preview_zh": "警方表示，这名男子身份尚未确认，年龄据信在近40岁或40岁出头。先有两名男子在路边接近他，随后更大一群人对他实施殴打。他被当场宣布死亡，警方已就谋杀立案调查。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 732, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/75/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 81.2, "size_bytes": 488160, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 238, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/75/en_b2_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 82.4, "size_bytes": 495360, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 238, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/75/en_b2_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/75/en_b2_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 87.8, "size_bytes": 527760, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 238, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/75/en_b2_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/75/en_b2_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 75.95, "size_bytes": 456624, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 238, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/75/en_b2_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/75/en_b2_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 83.2, "size_bytes": 500112, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 238, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/75/en_b2_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@5e0dbb9/content/data/versions/744.json", "paragraphs": ["According to police, the man, who has not been identified, was believed to be in his late 30s or early 40s. Two men first approached him by the roadside before a larger group attacked him. He was pronounced dead at the scene, and officers have opened a murder investigation.", "The motive has not yet been established. Provincial police spokesperson Robert Netshiunda told the BBC that they cannot speculate about why the man was killed, adding that more details would be released once they had been verified.", "The attack follows a wave of protests against immigrants in South Africa this year. Earlier this month, shops and cars were set on fire in Durban and in Soweto, near Johannesburg. The government has urged demonstrators to act peacefully while accepting that immigration reforms are needed.", "South Africa has struggled with xenophobic attacks for nearly two decades. In 2008, more than 60 people were killed and tens of thousands were displaced. The unrest comes amid widespread poverty, deep inequality and unemployment affecting about a third of the workforce.", "Migrants are often accused of taking jobs and adding to crime, although researchers say such broad claims are not supported by evidence. Despite its economic problems, South Africa remains a main destination for migrants seeking work and safety."], "paragraphs_zh": ["警方表示，这名男子身份尚未确认，年龄据信在近40岁或40岁出头。先有两名男子在路边接近他，随后更大一群人对他实施殴打。他被当场宣布死亡，警方已就谋杀立案调查。", "作案动机目前尚未确定。省警方发言人罗伯特·内齐温达对BBC表示，他们不能猜测这名男子被杀的原因，并称更多细节将在核实后公布。", "这起袭击发生之前，南非今年出现了一波反移民抗议。本月早些时候，德班和约翰内斯堡附近的索韦托都有商店和汽车被纵火焚烧。政府敦促示威者和平行动，同时也承认需要进行移民改革。", "近二十年来，南非一直难以摆脱排外袭击。2008年，在针对外国人的大规模袭击中，60多人丧生，数万人流离失所。此次骚乱的背景是普遍贫困、严重不平等以及影响约三分之一劳动力的失业问题。", "移民常被指责抢走工作、加剧犯罪，但研究人员表示，这类笼统的说法并无证据支持。尽管经济困难，南非仍是移民寻求工作与安全的主要目的地之一。"], "body": "According to police, the man, who has not been identified, was believed to be in his late 30s or early 40s. Two men first approached him by the roadside before a larger group attacked him. He was pronounced dead at the scene, and officers have opened a murder investigation.\n\nThe motive has not yet been established. Provincial police spokesperson Robert Netshiunda told the BBC that they cannot speculate about why the man was killed, adding that more details would be released once they had been verified.\n\nThe attack follows a wave of protests against immigrants in South Africa this year. Earlier this month, shops and cars were set on fire in Durban and in Soweto, near Johannesburg. The government has urged demonstrators to act peacefully while accepting that immigration reforms are needed.\n\nSouth Africa has struggled with xenophobic attacks for nearly two decades. In 2008, more than 60 people were killed and tens of thousands were displaced. The unrest comes amid widespread poverty, deep inequality and unemployment affecting about a third of the workforce.\n\nMigrants are often accused of taking jobs and adding to crime, although researchers say such broad claims are not supported by evidence. Despite its economic problems, South Africa remains a main destination for migrants seeking work and safety.", "body_zh": "警方表示，这名男子身份尚未确认，年龄据信在近40岁或40岁出头。先有两名男子在路边接近他，随后更大一群人对他实施殴打。他被当场宣布死亡，警方已就谋杀立案调查。\n\n作案动机目前尚未确定。省警方发言人罗伯特·内齐温达对BBC表示，他们不能猜测这名男子被杀的原因，并称更多细节将在核实后公布。\n\n这起袭击发生之前，南非今年出现了一波反移民抗议。本月早些时候，德班和约翰内斯堡附近的索韦托都有商店和汽车被纵火焚烧。政府敦促示威者和平行动，同时也承认需要进行移民改革。\n\n近二十年来，南非一直难以摆脱排外袭击。2008年，在针对外国人的大规模袭击中，60多人丧生，数万人流离失所。此次骚乱的背景是普遍贫困、严重不平等以及影响约三分之一劳动力的失业问题。\n\n移民常被指责抢走工作、加剧犯罪，但研究人员表示，这类笼统的说法并无证据支持。尽管经济困难，南非仍是移民寻求工作与安全的主要目的地之一。", "text": "According to police, the man, who has not been identified, was believed to be in his late 30s or early 40s. Two men first approached him by the roadside before a larger group attacked him. He was pronounced dead at the scene, and officers have opened a murder investigation. The motive has not yet been established. Provincial police spokesperson Robert Netshiunda told the BBC that they cannot speculate about why the man was killed, adding that more details would be released once they had been verified. The attack follows a wave of protests against immigrants in South Africa this year. Earlier this month, shops and cars were set on fire in Durban and in Soweto, near Johannesburg. The government has urged demonstrators to act peacefully while accepting that immigration reforms are needed. South Africa has struggled with xenophobic attacks for nearly two decades. In 2008, more than 60 people were killed and tens of thousands were displaced. The unrest comes amid widespread poverty, deep inequality and unemployment affecting about a third of the workforce. Migrants are often accused of taking jobs and adding to crime, although researchers say such broad claims are not supported by evidence. Despite its economic problems, South Africa remains a main destination for migrants seeking work and safety.", "vocab": [{"word": "foreign national", "pos": "noun", "zh": "外籍人士", "note": "新闻用语，比 foreigner 更正式", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "beat to death", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "殴打致死", "note": "被动形式 be beaten to death", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "pronounced dead", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "被宣布死亡", "note": "常用于现场急救后的官方说法", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "motive", "pos": "noun", "zh": "动机", "note": "犯罪新闻高频词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "launch an investigation", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "展开调查", "note": "也可说 open an investigation", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "speculate", "pos": "verb", "zh": "猜测，推测", "note": "常与 about/on 连用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "verified", "pos": "adj", "zh": "已核实的", "note": "动词 verify 的过去分词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "demonstrator", "pos": "noun", "zh": "示威者", "note": "对应动词 demonstrate", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "xenophobic", "pos": "adj", "zh": "排外的，仇外的", "note": "名词形式 xenophobia", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "displaced", "pos": "adj", "zh": "被迫离开家园的，流离失所的", "note": "常指因冲突或灾害", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "inequality", "pos": "noun", "zh": "不平等", "note": "常与 poverty 并列", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "repatriate", "pos": "verb", "zh": "遣返，使回国", "note": "文中作被动 repatriated", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "fetched_at": "2026-10-23T00:06:23.045368", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "According", "s": 0.25, "e": 0.675, "sm": 250, "em": 675, "cs": 0, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "to", "s": 0.675, "e": 0.775, "sm": 675, "em": 774, "cs": 10, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "police", "s": 0.775, "e": 1.5, "sm": 775, "em": 1500, "cs": 13, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": ",", "s": 1.5, "e": 1.6, "sm": 1500, "em": 1600, "cs": 19, "ce": 20, "s